Fundamental property models, derivatives and verification (@th-property-model: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/IAPWS-95-Fundamental-Water-Formulation.lingua#r_4JH7YVKGMCC4R7MK1F5S1XY90Z", #source "../sources/IAPWS-IF97-Industrial-Water-and-Steam.lingua#r_7THV30AN6Q693AJKH3W6ZSG13Y", #source "../sources/Open-Thermophysical-Library-Bell-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_33XEMZDJ2BMYZ0GDFGWDTV1C95", #source "../sources/CoolProp-Thermophysical-Property-Methods.lingua#r_2QYM459W81KPNJK37RHJ6VB9R1", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../practice/Compare-water-and-fluid-property-models-with-primary-data.lingua#r_73W5C0HV0M8PZT25HEVJ0CMJJZ", #fluid-dynamics "../../fluid-dynamics/compressible/Sound-speed-acoustic-impedance-and-linear-waves.lingua#r_66QA17NADDVJNJWKZKFJF9TX7N") { r_764YPYD3A83WPVMG0N594Y9W71
**Read:** [IAPWS-95 — fundamental water properties](../sources/IAPWS-95-Fundamental-Water-Formulation.lingua#r_4JH7YVKGMCC4R7MK1F5S1XY90Z), the complete release; [IAPWS-IF97 — industrial water and steam](../sources/IAPWS-IF97-Industrial-Water-and-Steam.lingua#r_7THV30AN6Q693AJKH3W6ZSG13Y), the complete release and applicable backward equations; [Open thermophysical property evaluation — Bell and colleagues](../sources/Open-Thermophysical-Library-Bell-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_33XEMZDJ2BMYZ0GDFGWDTV1C95), the complete primary paper; [CoolProp — thermophysical property models and methods](../sources/CoolProp-Thermophysical-Property-Methods.lingua#r_2QYM459W81KPNJK37RHJ6VB9R1), the complete relevant property-model documentation.

Use one consistent fundamental equation to derive pressure, entropy, enthalpy and response functions. Identify its independent variables, reference terms, fluid composition, phase range and numerical inversion. Thermodynamic-property accuracy and transport-property accuracy are separate: an equation of state does not alone determine conductivity or viscosity.

Read all of [IAPWS-95 — fundamental water properties](../sources/IAPWS-95-Fundamental-Water-Formulation.lingua#r_4JH7YVKGMCC4R7MK1F5S1XY90Z) and [IAPWS-IF97 — industrial water and steam](../sources/IAPWS-IF97-Industrial-Water-and-Steam.lingua#r_7THV30AN6Q693AJKH3W6ZSG13Y) and work their numerical check values independently. Compare direct evaluations, inverse state requests and saturation states. Examine region-boundary tolerances, derivative behavior and root selection before embedding a library in a cycle calculation.

Record the actual [CoolProp — thermophysical property models and methods](../sources/CoolProp-Thermophysical-Property-Methods.lingua#r_2QYM459W81KPNJK37RHJ6VB9R1) version and backend, and reconstruct the full [Open thermophysical property evaluation — Bell and colleagues](../sources/Open-Thermophysical-Library-Bell-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_33XEMZDJ2BMYZ0GDFGWDTV1C95) method. Test units and reference-state changes explicitly. A package's successful return does not prove that the requested state is stable, within its model range or representative of a real mixture.

**Continue:** [Compare fluid property models with primary data](../practice/Compare-water-and-fluid-property-models-with-primary-data.lingua#r_73W5C0HV0M8PZT25HEVJ0CMJJZ).

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer](../Thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer.lingua#r_6KQBZNJM6WNV9A69R3DZY1NH7E).

